  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>sum-geometric-series-i-q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A school notice is passed from learner to learner in rounds. In each round, the number of learners who hear the notice for the first time is multiplied by the same number, so the numbers form a geometric progression (GP). In round {@p@}, {@tp@} learners hear it for the first time. In round {@q@}, {@tq@} learners hear it for the first time.</p>

<p>(a) Find the common ratio, \(r\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the number of learners who hear the notice in round 1, which is the first term, \(a\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Find the total number of learners who have heard the notice after {@N@} rounds.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Find the number of learners who hear the notice from round {@s@} to round {@N@}, including both rounds.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Round {@p@} has {@tp@} learners and round {@q@} has {@tq@} learners. The numbers form a geometric progression (GP).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>Use \( T_n = ar^{n-1} \) for the two rounds.</p>
<p>\[ ar^{ {@p-1@} } = {@tp@} \qquad \text{(equation 1)} \]</p>
<p>\[ ar^{ {@q-1@} } = {@tq@} \qquad \text{(equation 2)} \]</p>
<p>Divide equation 2 by equation 1. This eliminates \(a\):</p>
<p>\[ \frac{ar^{ {@q-1@} }}{ar^{ {@p-1@} }} = \frac{ {@tq@} }{ {@tp@} } \]</p>
<p>\[ r^{2} = {@quot@} \]</p>
<p>Since \(r\) is positive, \( r = {@ta1@} \).</p>

<p>(b) <strong>First term:</strong></p>
<p>Put \( r = {@r@} \) into equation 1:</p>
<p>\[ a \times {@r^(p-1)@} = {@tp@} \]</p>
<p>\[ a = \frac{ {@tp@} }{ {@r^(p-1)@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Total after {@N@} rounds:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@N@} } = \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{ {@N@} } - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = \frac{ {@a@} \times {@r^N - 1@} }{ {@r - 1@} } = {@ta3@} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>Rounds {@s@} to {@N@}:</strong></p>
<p>This is all {@N@} rounds without the first {@s-1@} rounds. So we need \( S_{ {@s-1@} } \):</p>
<p>\[ S_{ {@s-1@} } = \frac{ {@a@}\left({@r@}^{ {@s-1@} } - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = {@Ss1@} \]</p>
<p>Subtract:</p>
<p>\[ {@SN@} - {@Ss1@} = {@ta4@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
